[{:db/id "q-127427/selection/d77ac287c521165226f56ec0f3f6a1bb6c6d5367472df808f23909fc628dc0f2" :answer/id #uuid "c7003c81-e6bf-54ce-ba19-e4bea2c5efd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127427/selection/0e60e7e61992c214034a71fcf8b61ecb6891dc3d7518889ce1a59c54d7932852" :answer/id #uuid "4eda1903-6379-565f-99c0-d8768637792a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127427/selection/24602c7d574476dd139a6525a4360fbf0bf303ca116ff780371ea95ec483bca9" :answer/id #uuid "a5bbbab0-72dd-50cf-8c36-0102e6564c06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127427/selection/afa9110b4e3cc37d8cfb47b621f812330d4dea2bab955f8b7a2eb4d903dcaab5" :answer/id #uuid "da08c350-3fc6-51b3-9576-20e159e4d25d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127427/selection/48fae2af272cb946fddc8452a42780253adbace166f9945eaed729aebd9e0a04" :answer/id #uuid "283861f5-43ed-5426-be14-76882e7738b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127427/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "712c7078-6f11-550c-9ba9-1fe27bfa93b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127427/selection/afa9110b4e3cc37d8cfb47b621f812330d4dea2bab955f8b7a2eb4d903dcaab5" :answer-field/choices ["q-127427/selection/d77ac287c521165226f56ec0f3f6a1bb6c6d5367472df808f23909fc628dc0f2" "q-127427/selection/0e60e7e61992c214034a71fcf8b61ecb6891dc3d7518889ce1a59c54d7932852" "q-127427/selection/24602c7d574476dd139a6525a4360fbf0bf303ca116ff780371ea95ec483bca9" "q-127427/selection/afa9110b4e3cc37d8cfb47b621f812330d4dea2bab955f8b7a2eb4d903dcaab5" "q-127427/selection/48fae2af272cb946fddc8452a42780253adbace166f9945eaed729aebd9e0a04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127427" :question/id #uuid "dd39f385-6d0a-55b7-bb7b-d5fcb8c4110d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127427" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+({e}^{t})^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{e}^{2t}+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127427/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc0992a-423e-5023-98d5-9d53c3b77788"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127427"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33728"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/d162245ac19c3ef9ae63d602fb4e188ddfd241a1a604304f6c272c3902ce1e93.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=\\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-127419/selection/b2cd2de00bde0dd8a255566828ca33952f71e2903f234631ad8514ac2ceb1d87" :answer/id #uuid "424f708e-dd4b-5a83-ab98-85698b689593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127419/selection/de051ced2234c5f3b709d52a611e53d6b2c5f1d0f16e6f9a8104842ab87bf5a4" :answer/id #uuid "54272ead-9698-5568-a8df-0c13734955ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127419/selection/502a8fa5498b9cf632d8a1117d0d9c8bbd97691bd61de6fb1c94574f3e1739c7" :answer/id #uuid "fe2ce299-a7cf-5947-928c-e7aff3072ce3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127419/selection/41605b1944e60ad1fa09dbc3f4fa906817a40adfb0505ce00c5941ba72c570e5" :answer/id #uuid "613d3166-f0dc-57b8-a194-ee02be2dd008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127419/selection/c4a8be3cc5789bbc429e89ae30e33797066d1282f4512e87d0b3b7ab27c90adf" :answer/id #uuid "3ac019c9-b53c-5b84-bb5b-95e2579c358b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡t+9}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127419/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2478357d-1708-51a5-b69c-e1231f554fbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127419/selection/502a8fa5498b9cf632d8a1117d0d9c8bbd97691bd61de6fb1c94574f3e1739c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-127419/selection/b2cd2de00bde0dd8a255566828ca33952f71e2903f234631ad8514ac2ceb1d87" "q-127419/selection/de051ced2234c5f3b709d52a611e53d6b2c5f1d0f16e6f9a8104842ab87bf5a4" "q-127419/selection/502a8fa5498b9cf632d8a1117d0d9c8bbd97691bd61de6fb1c94574f3e1739c7" "q-127419/selection/41605b1944e60ad1fa09dbc3f4fa906817a40adfb0505ce00c5941ba72c570e5" "q-127419/selection/c4a8be3cc5789bbc429e89ae30e33797066d1282f4512e87d0b3b7ab27c90adf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127419" :question/id #uuid "20f7dd35-57f3-5479-bd92-ca0b991a0b49" :question/math-academy-id "q-127419" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ from $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127419/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc0992a-423e-5023-98d5-9d53c3b77788"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127419"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33706/selection/1e2baf16972c5dc042aa2df703b1f6e19d1aa9e38c14deb513b63ea19b2d301c" :answer/id #uuid "4bdfd2b7-5937-5894-a9d7-95142f166eb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33706/selection/17fcd0d73006df1e29882e050888a2fe3a7c962fd9467d290660ca27fa2426b9" :answer/id #uuid "66642048-bc22-5eea-b2ad-df31d6dcb513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33706/selection/de13286035db3f567699ae4e73b393a17b0c11cb929f48a335ad08ce2f02e083" :answer/id #uuid "42d6d23d-8ed6-5c5e-bd3d-c1c800b0b289" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33706/selection/a0bb3b03f64cf6e1f5afbcac9043ea3e1e97e5249880d585264daab7e18b825f" :answer/id #uuid "9aea866e-c775-59eb-b0e6-a9ab07ab5ee6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33706/selection/7e7b35fd1e6e0509c26f9055f70dec74d0a2c807733b37815a0a757929ea2d26" :answer/id #uuid "cfa0888b-178c-5e4a-b01c-f23d3f494331" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33706/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "008c720e-beaf-5586-b0fb-04ddedb5f59d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33706/selection/17fcd0d73006df1e29882e050888a2fe3a7c962fd9467d290660ca27fa2426b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-33706/selection/1e2baf16972c5dc042aa2df703b1f6e19d1aa9e38c14deb513b63ea19b2d301c" "q-33706/selection/17fcd0d73006df1e29882e050888a2fe3a7c962fd9467d290660ca27fa2426b9" "q-33706/selection/de13286035db3f567699ae4e73b393a17b0c11cb929f48a335ad08ce2f02e083" "q-33706/selection/a0bb3b03f64cf6e1f5afbcac9043ea3e1e97e5249880d585264daab7e18b825f" "q-33706/selection/7e7b35fd1e6e0509c26f9055f70dec74d0a2c807733b37815a0a757929ea2d26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33706" :question/id #uuid "214d5c25-f05c-5b96-87cf-f66e123da8aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-33706" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/10ee30ddf508bf985e1c3a41491818723b57301412a5514e4a39c3bc13518acd.png)\n\nWhich integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,2-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=\\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33706/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc0992a-423e-5023-98d5-9d53c3b77788"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33706"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33862"] :question/problem "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)={e}^{t}(\\,i+2\\,j+t\\,k)$ from  $t=1$ to $t=2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+2{e}^{t}\\,j+(t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(2{e}^{t})^{2}+({e}^{t}(t+1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}({t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}(1+4+{t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-77070/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "878ba0f5-86a7-5499-95b6-b8ee697520de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77070/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "06d3dc67-08b7-53d1-8906-8b5c24424730" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77070/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "674875bc-4f35-53fb-95ce-a14b696d5b55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77070/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "fa50f169-2f56-5e7e-b650-02ae3a23d7f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77070/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "40f8ac1e-ce59-56b8-a08d-1cfe300e55f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77070/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b764e5d-17a2-5ddd-9a42-762f9b132663" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77070/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-77070/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-77070/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-77070/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-77070/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-77070/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77070" :question/id #uuid "af50538c-8630-50c4-8711-30786b7c74cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-77070" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/e6de928031610e2aaf55e3dd753449f766e7dc028a6618087e7489224a73ea7d.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-77070/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e310cbe-9d6b-5bc4-960a-8813333bc8be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127573/selection/6389cb97be2c2d22d6cc89d984fff3d7e6cbb4d13a52b4a8057f5775b72bc154" :answer/id #uuid "b9cc2330-9cd2-5d53-b054-0f32f557c8dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi /2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127573/selection/7dbcba444ae21af974533c30459d043b0d8742bee1e58932c2b9bd1bf30b19c0" :answer/id #uuid "18d0ae59-913f-5120-b95f-494f10556d02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127573/selection/d0cc8d0b58206cb3f047c023afd9abe8a8624b60673d6672dcdda51c0dd66379" :answer/id #uuid "915ff0ce-2deb-597a-807a-bff8bac385cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({e}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127573/selection/35a61b0ce34fd3e4622a5db4eab84c634eb3a3a73ec9f00b8ef489d7be12926f" :answer/id #uuid "1191db6c-09ca-5e01-9129-050a63648dbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi /2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127573/selection/553c66e627a7db04964d805f138127145e4d68addd35ceb210e9f46399f3eab8" :answer/id #uuid "75a005ca-6f70-5830-acaf-5ff9cbc7f017" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi }-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127573/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "662f2f2b-9e63-53a0-acac-fbeeeddf9d25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127573/selection/7dbcba444ae21af974533c30459d043b0d8742bee1e58932c2b9bd1bf30b19c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-127573/selection/6389cb97be2c2d22d6cc89d984fff3d7e6cbb4d13a52b4a8057f5775b72bc154" "q-127573/selection/7dbcba444ae21af974533c30459d043b0d8742bee1e58932c2b9bd1bf30b19c0" "q-127573/selection/d0cc8d0b58206cb3f047c023afd9abe8a8624b60673d6672dcdda51c0dd66379" "q-127573/selection/35a61b0ce34fd3e4622a5db4eab84c634eb3a3a73ec9f00b8ef489d7be12926f" "q-127573/selection/553c66e627a7db04964d805f138127145e4d68addd35ceb210e9f46399f3eab8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127573" :question/id #uuid "e766b230-ebad-5e20-ae10-19faeacf27a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-127573" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/162c0d0310cbbb533c30af373820751fc6c5a447127958486571224d7f8ac07a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{t}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|{e}^{t}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127573/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e310cbe-9d6b-5bc4-960a-8813333bc8be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127573"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77220/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "8dc5d1c1-2837-56b3-a302-3c40a0d6d9f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77220/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "315b78a7-a9f4-56a3-bbaa-a33dcb4a81ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77220/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "b4a975d7-d0c2-5d3f-a8db-b9dd175a8498" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77220/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "b0dceaa5-1a7b-5113-bf8d-144eeb02d429" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77220/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "fdcdaab1-718e-5f81-9526-2351f4961596" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77220/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ddaa2dc-72c3-542f-b301-04ce5fa97c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77220/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-77220/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-77220/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-77220/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-77220/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-77220/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77220" :question/id #uuid "02904945-e53d-5a5a-8b80-5ae0efb5f8d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-77220" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/2efa774a3a7e97c23f695cfbdf681b53df055b8a84b84e2729af0a565841aeb7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,,4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2(4-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77220/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e310cbe-9d6b-5bc4-960a-8813333bc8be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77220"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-77065"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/b614e2c3e6abf0d7ddb8399aa7ea78b7a0e618a965ee7b5481edf08310a45031.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-3t,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=1$ to $t=2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-3,\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}-3)^{2}+(6t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}-18{t}^{2}+9+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+18{t}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}+3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{3}+3t){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(8+6)-(1+3) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-77068/selection/f003b95a6c7a22f536ec799844670c061a2d01da9486469d5da5d96020e58645" :answer/id #uuid "a216650d-e61d-5cdf-b2f1-4504b6fb8c51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77068/selection/32e65fe743d0d028abb30010be473c4445ce2177c6c283fcc4d5963ada5dca86" :answer/id #uuid "f6ed477a-0abb-5c04-a885-8fa44e428a1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77068/selection/b11548864a68119ffee7fb9a515e2fde8c71940e5e93e132601eb89ba3f4b840" :answer/id #uuid "d95e2f01-8f4a-575a-9909-0b593c2a483f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77068/selection/7c07b5a887efbe98f55eee9ae2a25f57d8e31af3fc3fa15a8de286f0ef5b8848" :answer/id #uuid "1665e8a7-30b8-53fa-b649-757c85f99d95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77068/selection/5576b1ae498ee1e3443c18b29beceee5848cdd1190d5966938414565fd118318" :answer/id #uuid "b74984cb-7151-5645-9619-17779a1dacb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}+{e}^{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77068/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e37b7c7-1a63-5984-b66d-212510102dfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77068/selection/b11548864a68119ffee7fb9a515e2fde8c71940e5e93e132601eb89ba3f4b840" :answer-field/choices ["q-77068/selection/f003b95a6c7a22f536ec799844670c061a2d01da9486469d5da5d96020e58645" "q-77068/selection/32e65fe743d0d028abb30010be473c4445ce2177c6c283fcc4d5963ada5dca86" "q-77068/selection/b11548864a68119ffee7fb9a515e2fde8c71940e5e93e132601eb89ba3f4b840" "q-77068/selection/7c07b5a887efbe98f55eee9ae2a25f57d8e31af3fc3fa15a8de286f0ef5b8848" "q-77068/selection/5576b1ae498ee1e3443c18b29beceee5848cdd1190d5966938414565fd118318"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77068" :question/id #uuid "8ca4a02e-469e-5c53-9830-ef767df61f51" :question/math-academy-id "q-77068" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/54cd1a0532bbdbe76bd81d5ad737f6d3e9f5293d08ea78758865b3b71850e346.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2},\\,2t⟩$ from $t=1$ to $t=e.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t}-t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{t}-t)}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-2+{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+2+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{t}+t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{1}{t}+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2})-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-77068/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e310cbe-9d6b-5bc4-960a-8813333bc8be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77068"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76914/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "612599a2-0d24-5584-8ec9-03156e2ea4e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76914/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "f0e3a282-a6ab-5493-8dad-e6858e2cc307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76914/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "d4f136fa-e4dd-52af-a412-280899af0845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76914/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "104f25b4-0991-5fa2-a86e-714183a38770" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76914/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "137cc6ce-1302-55b8-93da-b31da784beb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76914/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3670a8d8-8690-5738-a2b3-cb0bb5b0a50c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76914/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-76914/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-76914/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-76914/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-76914/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-76914/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76914" :question/id #uuid "5bcd5987-bf48-5940-9557-fe98a5e45bbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-76914" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2},\\,2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,3t,\\,4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}+(3t)^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡2t+9{t}^{2}+16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+9{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-76914/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1889ba1a-09d4-5021-9ed2-3e531f8d5ef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76914"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76906/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "0038e453-423d-585c-9ead-2b5ff1f2baf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76906/selection/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer/id #uuid "53517ea3-26c4-5902-be5e-7023b9c68892" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76906/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "a43dd25b-f9c5-5b3c-bc3a-355433d5b591" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76906/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "f5b1533c-c1d2-5059-825f-ba540a3714d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76906/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1e072aa8-0925-56f3-ade4-e8a9dd23122e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76906/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5acc5f4-e4cb-5ddd-9fc2-1da017060484" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76906/selection/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer-field/choices ["q-76906/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-76906/selection/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" "q-76906/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-76906/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-76906/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76906" :question/id #uuid "23862600-8c37-5abe-8c3d-0dc47feee1b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-76906" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,4,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2t)}^{2}+0+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\,t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2\\sqrt{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76906/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1889ba1a-09d4-5021-9ed2-3e531f8d5ef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76906"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33779"] :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom $t=1$ to $t=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+3{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,3].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-77064/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "9a22f314-d891-5169-9d3f-d4d1f4eb8a7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77064/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "e32967c6-13f5-5773-a742-212b2ba5fe59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77064/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "73d98c4b-73b9-599d-9fa3-ead0e0a15b0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77064/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "3b649431-c3be-51cd-9dc2-071bc864f0f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77064/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e7b4a854-0041-5a85-8731-a0328b89dee1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77064/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b56fc8c5-8aac-5229-b630-e3cc573b124a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77064/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-77064/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-77064/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-77064/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-77064/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-77064/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77064" :question/id #uuid "69c5e2d0-9a19-5b71-8a53-1d2aae0ee046" :question/math-academy-id "q-77064" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨10,\\,\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(10),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}+1+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t)|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9+3-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-77064/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1889ba1a-09d4-5021-9ed2-3e531f8d5ef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77064"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76908/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "3e0b251b-a2f3-51f4-857d-e33813608a90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76908/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "278f23d4-19d4-5318-bf64-9ca7749d8f60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76908/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "b846764f-9a58-5734-b107-fe85d252b7e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76908/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "0499fa2b-b337-50a1-b3a8-2113b215492d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76908/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "a1091c3e-1b66-5305-b116-8a3e95af242f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76908/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b38e44a8-b383-57df-85ce-af7c3d0ac054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76908/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer-field/choices ["q-76908/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" "q-76908/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" "q-76908/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-76908/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-76908/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76908" :question/id #uuid "3830e6d2-8ce6-57ca-aeaf-b00b3e2423bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-76908" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2t,\\,2{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}+{(2{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}+4{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(1+2{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =1+2{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(1+2{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(t+\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3})|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3+18-0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76908/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1889ba1a-09d4-5021-9ed2-3e531f8d5ef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76908"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3063"] :question/problem "Write down the integral that gives the arc length of the curve  $\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle 3 \\sin t, \\: 2\\sin 2t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =\\dfrac {3\\pi} 2$  to $t = 2\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/574a16e843a9c81e5fc9ddbbe2c0dc2c308ffcac4991bcbf48c7f45b4871c93b.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3064"] :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf g (t) = \\langle 3 - 2 \\sin 2t, \\: 1 - 2\\cos 2t \\rangle$ from $t=\\dfrac \\pi 3$ to $\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/29c97e5963d451cc389944ef113764b2d15998448e773a02bb98c062207c2860.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡2t+16{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6303"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/8573aedcd26cba038b2db072560cd3d6ba7676542888a2d9b8a356713eaf6724.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\: \\cos t, \\: t \\rangle$\nfrom  $t =0$ to $t = 2\\pi.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\sqrt{2}\\,t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
